body:
I extend the examples.

`execute()` method of the command. Let's make it just report the connection name.

```php
    public function execute(Arguments $args, ConsoleIo $io): int
    {
        /** @var \App\Model\Table\MailBoxesTable $MailBoxesTable */
        $MailBoxesTable = $this->fetchTable('MailBoxes');

        $io->out($MailBoxesTable->getConnection()->configName());

        return self::CODE_SUCCESS;
    }
```

Some tests:
```php
    public function setUp(): void
    {
        parent::setUp();

        $this->MailBoxesTable = $this->fetchTable('MailBoxes');
    }

    #[Test]
    #[RunInSeparateProcess]
    public function testInSeparateProcess(): void
    {
        $this->exec('fetch_mails -v');
        $this->assertOutputContains('test');
    }

    #[Test]
    public function testNotInSeparateProcess(): void
    {
        $this->exec('fetch_mails -v');
        $this->assertOutputContains('test');
    }
```

Outcome:
```
1) App\Test\TestCase\Command\FetchMailsCommandTest::testInSeparateProcess
Failed asserting that 'test' is in output..
actual result:
default
```
(`testNotInSeparateProcess()` is ok instead)

Instead if:
```php
        $this->MailBoxesTable = $this->fetchTable('MailBoxes', ['connection' => ConnectionManager::get('test')]);
```
everything's ok:
```
OK (2 tests, 2 assertions)
```
